# nanopb field options for navamesh.proto.
#
# Firmware-side only. nanopb reads this to size fields at compile time; the Pi's
# navamesh_pb2.py is built by plain protoc, which ignores it entirely. That is why
# this file is NOT duplicated into the Navamesh repo the way navamesh.proto is --
# only the .proto has to stay byte-identical across the two.
#
# Without a max_size here nanopb emits a pb_callback_t for the string, which means
# hand-written encode/decode callbacks for a field that is a fixed short constant.

# APP_VERSION is Meshtastic's long version string: "2.7.20.200289a" today, 14 chars.
# 20 leaves room for a longer hash or a two-digit minor without a proto change, and
# matches the spirit of DeviceMetadata.firmware_version[18] upstream. Includes the
# NUL terminator.
navamesh.NavameshAck.firmware_version max_size:20
